# The ONLY real gate on this test: read_verilog rejects `pipeReg[i][j].valid`
# outright (syntax error on member access into an element of a 2-D unpacked
# array), so the ordinary verilog-vs-uhdm comparison cannot run at all.
# read_slang resolves the shape correctly.
#
# Without the fix the shift arm's `pipeReg[i][j-1] <= pipeReg[i][j]` never
# reaches the `valid`/`dep` fields -- they hold their reset mux forever while
# `ptr` shifts -- and this miter finds a counterexample within 5 cycles.
# memory_map is needed because read_slang infers a $mem for the 2-D array and
# read_uhdm expands it; satgen has no model for $mem_v2.
read_uhdm slpp_all/surelog.uhdm
hierarchy -check -top pipe_elem_whole_and_field_arms
prep -top pipe_elem_whole_and_field_arms -flatten
memory_map; opt -fast; async2sync; setundef -undriven -zero
rename pipe_elem_whole_and_field_arms gold
design -stash gold
read_slang dut.sv --top pipe_elem_whole_and_field_arms
hierarchy -check -top pipe_elem_whole_and_field_arms
prep -top pipe_elem_whole_and_field_arms -flatten
memory_map; opt -fast; async2sync; setundef -undriven -zero
rename pipe_elem_whole_and_field_arms gate
design -stash gate
design -copy-from gold -as gold gold
design -copy-from gate -as gate gate
miter -equiv -flatten -make_assert gold gate miter
hierarchy -top miter
sat -verify -prove-asserts -seq 5 -set-init-zero miter
